  "conclusion": "V7 substantially reduces fitted tip lag and same-time position/orientation error. After startup, all recorded orientation samples are below 1 degree. Whole-pass orientation still fails at two startup samples (0.442/0.473 s, peak 1.095 degrees). The 20.050 mm window envelope does not establish 20 mm on every cycle: matched-cycle sampled stroke has median 18.350 mm and range 15.723-19.611 mm versus 20 mm planned. Full accuracy and repeatability remain unqualified.",
  "next_work": "Improve the finite startup transition and quantify cycle-to-cycle stroke/shape variation, including A6 response and actual dispatch cadence. Preserve the now-small steady phase error, all guard limits and independent tip validation requirements. Keep ILC deferred.",
  "limitations": [
    "Encoder-reconstructed tool pose with fixed base; no independent tip measurement and no specified tip-mm tolerance.",
    "Sequential trials have different preparation starts and control policies; this comparison does not isolate inertia or any single physical mechanism.",
    "Whole-window envelope combines extremes from different cycles. Per-cycle values are sampled extrema and may miss between-sample peaks.",
    "The 3.19 ms value is a fitted periodic position lag, not measured transport latency; it is shorter than the 27.39 ms median tick interval.",
    "Same-time orientation includes all 23 startup samples. No phase alignment is used for orientation acceptance.",
    "Formal analyzer retains manual-pause outcome and the 1-degree startup failure; interior diagnostics do not override acceptance.",
    "No controller, profile, firmware, guard or motor owner was changed during this review."
  ],
